    <div class="bench-copy">
      <p>
        Tako can handle <strong>heavy traffic</strong> even on modest hardware: one small VM served
        12.5k HTTPS 200 RPS at 5k concurrency, with <strong>zero client errors</strong> up to 20k concurrency.
        In the same public run, it outpaced <a href="https://caddyserver.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">Caddy</a> and <a href="https://www.envoyproxy.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">Envoy</a> under heavy HTTPS load.
      </p>
      <p>
        Tako is written in Rust: fast, memory-safe, and light on resources. Its proxy is built on <a href="https://blog.cloudflare.com/how-we-built-pingora-the-proxy-that-connects-cloudflare-to-the-internet/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pingora</a>, the Rust library behind Cloudflare&rsquo;s own network.
      </p>
      <a class="action doc-link" href="/performance/">Read the full report</a>
